[152.702165, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[152.702993, "o", "=== EXPORT_USERS.SH FIXES APPLIED ===\r\n\r\nDate: $(date)\r\nFixed by: System Administrator\r\n\r\nPROBLEM:\r\nAfter migration from flat passwd-style format to multi-file format, the export_users.sh\r\nscript was producing garbled CSV output with:\r\n- Emails merged with UIDs in the email column\r\n- Numeric GIDs instead of group names\r\n- Fields appearing in wrong columns\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSES (3 bugs identified):\r\n\r\n1. BUG #1: Wrong delimiter for emails.dat\r\n   - File uses TAB delimiter, script used SPACE delimiter\r\n   - Result: 'cut -d\" \"' failed, causing \"UID<TAB>email\" to be treated as one field\r\n   - FIX: Changed to use 'awk -F\"\\t\"' for proper tab-delimited parsing\r\n\r\n2. BUG #2: Sorting mismatch (removed unnecessary complexity)\r\n   - Original code sorted users alphabetically but emails numerically by UID\r\n   - Result: Line N of users didn't correspond to line N of emails\r\n   - FIX: Removed complex sort/paste logic, use direct UID-based lookup with awk\r\n\r\n3. BUG #3: Wrong delimiter for groups.dat\r\n   - File uses COLON delimiter,"]
[152.703069, "o", " awk used default (space/tab)\r\n   - Result: Entire \"GID:groupname:description\" treated as field 1\r\n   - FIX: Added '-F\":\"' to all awk commands processing groups.dat\r\n\r\nRESULTS:\r\n- All 800 users exported successfully (801 lines including header)\r\n- Clean CSV format with proper field separation\r\n- Group names properly resolved (engineering, devops, hr, etc.)\r\n- Email addresses clean without UID prefix\r\n- All supplementary groups resolved to names\r\n\r\nFILES:\r\n- export_users.sh.backup: Original broken script (saved for reference)\r\n- export_users.sh: Fixed script\r\n- export.csv: Clean export output (ready for use)\r\n- export_broken.csv: Sample broken output (for comparison)\r\n"]
[152.703183, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[152.703229, "o", "root@dbbebcf607a4:/home/user/admin# "]
